@baseUrl = http://localhost:5100

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Startup readiness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Development OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### Synthetic customer transactions (Development or Testing only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&transactionType=CardPurchase&fromDate=2026-11-01
X-Correlation-ID: demo-transaction-list

### Invalid query returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions?pageSize=101

### Owned synthetic transaction details (Development or Testing only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
X-Correlation-ID: demo-transaction-details

### Invalid transaction ID returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/not-a-guid

### Unknown or other-customer transaction returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099

### Evaluate owned transaction dispute eligibility (read-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/dispute-eligibility
X-Correlation-ID: demo-dispute-eligibility

### Valid DebiCheck: ordinary reversal blocked, authorization investigation remains available
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000011/dispute-eligibility

### Registered Mandate (fixed collection date; window eligibility depends on current date)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000014/dispute-eligibility

### Mismatched DebiCheck amount requires investigation
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000023/dispute-eligibility

### Authorization complaint enters manual review only; repeat submission returns 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000011",
  "reasonCode": "unauthorisedDebitOrder",
  "description": "I dispute the authorization recorded for this mandate."
}

### Malformed eligibility transaction ID returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/not-a-guid/dispute-eligibility

### Unknown or other-customer eligibility transaction returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099/dispute-eligibility

### Unknown route returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/not-a-route

### PR-08: submit an eligible synthetic EFT dispute (repeat submission returns 409)
# @name debitOrderCase
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "reasonCode": "duplicateCollection",
  "description": "This collection needs investigation for a duplicate debit."
}

### Run sequentially, changing command to VerifyMandate, RequestReversal, ExecuteReversal, Close
# Configure Simulation__DebitOrderKey in the API shell; REST Client must receive the same local value.
# Never commit the value or pass it to the customer frontend.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{debitOrderCase.response.body.$.id}}/debit-order-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Simulation-Key: {{$processEnv Simulation__DebitOrderKey}}
X-Correlation-ID: debit-order-demo

{ "command": "StartReview" }

### Ordinary customer processing is forbidden, even in Development
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{debitOrderCase.response.body.$.id}}/debit-order-simulations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "command": "ExecuteReversal" }

### Read the customer-owned timeline without simulator privileges
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{debitOrderCase.response.body.$.id}}